==Version history==
Masters were first introduced in the [[Path of Exile: Forsaken Masters|Forsaken Masters]] expansions. Completing [[Master (Forsaken Masters)|Forsaken Master]] missions granted experience towards unlocking [[crafting bench]] recipes and larger hideouts. Completing master missions also earned Favour used to unlock [[hideout]] decorations. Forsaken Masters also offered daily missions that granted extra experience.

In the [[Path of Exile: Betrayal|Betrayal]] expansion (3.5.0), the old masters (except Zana) were replaced. Despite 3.6.0 introduced new mechanic that used Zana as NPC, the poor reception of [[Synthesis league]] made the old Zana master mechanic retained in the game. She was replaced by [[Commander Kirac]] in version 3.17, but the master mechanic remained. Zana/Kirac's master mechanic is retired in 3.28 without replacement.

Masters used to be primarily encountered by earning master mission allowances by logging in once a day or completing a map, then enabling them to spawn them in your map. Each zone could only spawn one master at a time. These were changed later on.
